1
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:07,030
Lesson two, Bob returns home with bad news.

2
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:11,070
Bob tells his wife Susan that he lost his job.

3
00:00:11,539 --> 00:00:14,089
Susan suggests that he starred his own business.

4
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:16,809
What's the matter, dear?

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,489
Susan, I got canned today at work.

6
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:22,250
But Bob, you were Peter's right-hand man.

7
00:00:22,699 --> 00:00:24,349
Yes, and he stabbed me in the back.

8
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:26,049
Keep your chin up.

9
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:28,949
Maybe he'll change his mind and take you back.

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,949
When pigs fly, once he makes up his mind, he never changes it.

11
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,710
Besides, I told him off.

12
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:36,449
Look on the bright side.

13
00:00:36,719 --> 00:00:39,269
You won't have to set eyes on Peter ever again.

14
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:40,629
Thank goodness for that.

15
00:00:41,219 --> 00:00:41,990
Hang in there.

16
00:00:42,359 --> 00:00:44,170
I'm sure you won't be out of work for long.

17
00:00:44,439 --> 00:00:46,589
In the meantime, we'll have to live from hand to mouth.

18
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:48,530
Don't get too stressed out, Bob.

19
00:00:48,899 --> 00:00:49,869
We'll make ends meet.

20
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:52,750
I can always get a job in McDonald's as a last resort.

21
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:55,409
I don't think they're hiring right now.

22
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,070
If worse comes to worst, we can sell our home

23
00:00:57,920 --> 00:00:59,109
and move into a tent.

24
00:00:59,219 --> 00:01:00,329
Let's think big.

25
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:02,390
Maybe you can start your own business.

26
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,010
Easier said than done.

